  message: "Done (vocabulary half). Merged 945c063c3a (PR #345). The OTP linker no longer emits unregistered edge_types: otp_call/otp_cast folded to the registered dispatches_to edge_type + a new registered meta['mechanism'] key (values otp_call/otp_cast), at both emit blocks (Elixir CALL_TYPE_MAP + Erlang ERLANG_CALL_TYPE_MAP); meta.framework_dispatch=otp_genserver / call_type unchanged. Behavioral evidence (production-path): test_otp_linker.py — 44 pass, the edge assertions now require edge.edge_type=='dispatches_to' AND (edge.meta or {})['mechanism']=='otp_call'/'otp_cast' (e.g. lines 202/252/447/506/926/981 + the call/cast filter pair + the 2 Erlang-block equivalents). The L3 edge_type producer-coherence gate (test_no_strict_producer_violations_for_edge_type) is green — the linker now emits the literal 'dispatches_to' (registered), so the dict-indirected unregistered-value exposure is gone. dispatches_to was already registered; mechanism newly registered in axis_meta_keys. EXECUTION HALF SPLIT: the latent L3-walker blind-spot itself (static resolution of dict-indirection / tuple-unpack edge_type emit sites in producer_coherence._resolve_function_local/_resolve_simple_rhs) has NO remaining exploiter post-fold (the scope-sweep's claimed SCIP has_type/defined_by could not be reproduced) and is tracked as a focused preventive follow-up: WI-zigih. CHANGELOG ### Fixed updated."  # a769
